{"id":"word:hebrew:H441","type":"word","title":"אַלּוּף","subtitle":"H441 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"familiar ; a friend , also gentle ; hence, a bullock (as being tame; applied, although masculine, to a cow ); and so, a chieftain (as notable, like neat cattle)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אַלּוּף (H441) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: a-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 69 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אַלּוּף (ʼallûwph) means familiar ; a friend , also gentle ; hence, a bullock (as being tame; applied, although masculine, to a cow ); and so, a chieftain (as notable, like neat cattle) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 1 51."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אַלּוּף","transliteration":"ʼallûwph","pronunciation":"al-loof'","strong":"H441","lemmaId":"hebrew:H441","partOfSpeech":"a-m","forms":["אַלּ֥וּף","אַלּ֣וּף","אַלּוּפֵ֣י","אַלּֽוּף","אַלּוּפֵ֤י"],"morphs":[["HNcmsa",43],["HNcmpc",14],["HAamsa",3],["HNcmpc/Sp3mp",1],["HR/Ncmpc/Sp3mp",1],["HNcmsc",1],["HNcmpa",1],["HR/Aamsa",1],["HAamsc",1],["HNcmsc/Sp1cs",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"familiar ; a friend , also gentle ; hence, a bullock (as being tame; applied, although masculine, to a cow ); and so, a chieftain (as notable, like neat cattle)","usage":"captain, duke, (chief) friend, governor, guide, ox.","full":"H441. alluwph I. אַלּוּף adjective tame — ׳א absolute Micah 7:5 +; construct Prov 2:17 +; suffix אַלּוּפֵי Psa 55:14 ; plural אַלֻּפִים Jer 13:21 ; suffix אַלֻּפֵינוּ Psa 144:14 , etc.; &#8212; 1 tame, docile , אַלּוּף כֶּבֶשׂ a docile (gentle) lamb Jer 11:19 . 2. noun masculine friend, intimate Psa 55:14 (|| מְיֻדָּע ) Micah 7:5 (|| רֵעַ ) Prov 16:28 ; 17:9 ; Jer 13:21 ; of a woman's husband ׳א נְעוּרֶיהָ Prov 2:17 ; figurative of ׳י as husband of Judah, id. , Jer 3:4 . 3 i. q. I. אֶלֶף ; מְסֻבָּלִים אַלּוּפֵינוּ Psa 144:14 (i.e. cows). II. אַלּוּף noun masculine 1Chr 1:51 chief, chiliarch (denominative from II. אֶלֶף see Di Gen 36:15 ) &#8212; ׳א absolute 36:15 +; plural construct אַלּוּפֵי ( אַלֻּפֵי ) Exod 15:15 +; suffix אַלּוּפֵיהֶם Gen 36:19 , 30 — chief (tribal) of Edom 36:15 (5 t.) + 38 t. Genesis 36 (P); Exod 15:15 (E) 1Chr 1:51 (4 t.) + 9 t.; of Judah Zech 12:5-6 , so אַלֻּף 9:7 (in simile)","rootNote":"or (shortened) אַלֻּף ; from 502 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 1 51","keyReferences":["1Chr 1 51","1Chr 1 51","1Chr 1 51","1Chr 1 51","1Chr 1 52","1Chr 1 52","1Chr 1 52","1Chr 1 53"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":69,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 1 51","book":"1Chr","chapter":1,"verse":51,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַלּוּפֵ֣י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmpc"},{"reference":"1Chr 1 51","book":"1Chr","chapter":1,"verse":51,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַלּ֥וּף","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 1 51","book":"1Chr","chapter":1,"verse":51,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַלּ֥וּף","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 1 51","book":"1Chr","chapter":1,"verse":51,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַלּ֥וּף","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 1 52","book":"1Chr","chapter":1,"verse":52,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַלּ֧וּף","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 1 52","book":"1Chr","chapter":1,"verse":52,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַלּ֥וּף","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 1 52","book":"1Chr","chapter":1,"verse":52,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַלּ֥וּף","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 1 53","book":"1Chr","chapter":1,"verse":53,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַלּ֥וּף","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 1 53","book":"1Chr","chapter":1,"verse":53,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַלּ֥וּף","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 1 53","book":"1C